      ],
      "text": "Use multiplication and subtraction to solve this problem. Multiply 1 by the number of hours. Subtract that number from 70 (the temperature at 5:00 PM).",
      "example": "Example: In New York City, the temperature was 36 Fahrenheit at 11:00 PM. The temperature decreased six degrees every hour until 5:00 AM. What was the temperature at 5:00 AM?",
      "result": "Solution: Temperature at 11:00 PM = 36 Decrease in temperature per hour = 6 Number of hours of temperature decrease = 6 hours Temperature at 5:00 AM = (temperature at 11:00 PM) – (decrease in temperature per hour) (Number of hours of temperature decrease) Temperature at 5:00 AM = 36 (6 6) = 36 36 = 0",
      "productAdaptation": "Pause playback and gate the four answer controls while Help or its glossary is open; restore the same retry state on close."
